---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProductPicks from '../../components/ProductPicks.astro';
import { filters, partLabel } from '../../lib/data';
const rows = filters.map(f=>({d:f.dimensions.diameterIn,l:f.dimensions.lengthIn,name:`${f.brand} ${f.model}`,oem:f.oem,dt:(f.dimensions as any).diameterText,lt:(f.dimensions as any).lengthText,href:`/${f.brandSlug}/${f.modelSlug}/`}));
const examples: [string, string, string][] = [];
const seen = new Set<string>();
for (const f of filters) {
  const dt = (f.dimensions as any).diameterText as string, lt = (f.dimensions as any).lengthText as string;
  const key = `${dt}|${lt}`;
  if (seen.has(key)) continue;
  const pk = partLabel(f);
  if (!pk) continue;
  seen.add(key);
  examples.push([`${f.brand} ${pk}`, `${pk} spa filter`, `${dt} × ${lt}`]);
  if (examples.length >= 4) break;
}
---
<Base title="Spa Filter Size Lookup – Find a Hot Tub Filter by Dimensions" description="Look up a spa filter or hot tub filter by diameter and length, then confirm the end fittings before you order.">
<h1>Find a spa / hot tub filter by size</h1>
<p>Use this table when the part number on the end cap is worn off. Measure the <strong>diameter</strong> across the widest point of the pleats and the <strong>overall length</strong> from end to end, including a handle or a threaded nipple. Type either number, or both. The list stays empty until you do. Rows then stay visible when they are within 0.25 inches of what you typed, because catalog fractions (6", 10-1/2", 4-15/16") do not always match a tape to the hundredth.</p>
<p>Diameter and length are not the whole match. Unicel and Pleatco also print the top and the bottom: an open hole, a handle, a male slip, or a thread. Two cartridges can share a size and not share those ends. Caldera’s 7" × 10-3/4" parts are the usual example. After a row appears, open it and read the fittings before you order. The <a href="/guide/">measuring guide</a> is the longer version of these steps, and <a href="/guides/open-end-vs-threaded-hot-tub-filters/">open-end vs threaded filters</a> shows the patterns. If you can read any number at all, <a href="/">search that number</a> or use the <a href="/tools/cross-reference/">cross-reference lookup</a>. A readable number is more reliable than a measurement.</p>
<div class="card"><label>Diameter (in) <input id="d" type="number" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal"></label> <label>Length (in) <input id="l" type="number" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal"></label> <small>±0.25″ tolerance</small></div>
<p id="size-empty" hidden>Type a diameter or a length above. Matches within 0.25 inches are listed here, each linking to its cartridge page.</p>
<div class="tbl"><table id="t"><thead><tr><th>Filter</th><th>OEM</th><th>Dia</th><th>Length</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{rows.map(r=><tr data-d={r.d} data-l={r.l}><td><a href={r.href}>{r.name}</a></td><td>{r.oem}</td><td>{r.dt}</td><td>{r.lt}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p>A match in the table is a shortlist. Open the cartridge page for the cited OEM, Unicel, Pleatco and Filbur numbers, and for the retailer buttons. Brand guides that explain the common mix-ups: <a href="/guides/hot-spring-filter-sizes-by-collection/">Hot Spring</a>, <a href="/guides/caldera-filter-bottom-fittings/">Caldera</a>, <a href="/guides/bullfrog-threaded-and-coreless-filters/">Bullfrog</a>, <a href="/guides/sundance-and-jacuzzi-look-alike-filters/">Sundance and Jacuzzi</a>, <a href="/guides/intex-and-bestway-inflatable-spa-filters/">Intex and Bestway</a>. The full cited table is the <a href="/data/">dataset</a>.</p>
<ProductPicks heading="Search a few common sizes on Amazon" lead="These are examples of part numbers in this table, not a recommendation based on your measurement. Search only after the row you opened matches your diameter, length and ends." groups={[{h:'Part numbers from common sizes', search: examples}]} />
<script>
const d=document.getElementById('d') as HTMLInputElement, l=document.getElementById('l') as HTMLInputElement;
const empty=document.getElementById('size-empty');
const wrap=document.getElementById('t')?.closest('.tbl') as HTMLElement | null;
const f=()=>{
  const typed=d.value!==''||l.value!=='';
  let n=0;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('#t tbody tr').forEach(r=>{const ok=(i:HTMLInputElement,v:string)=>!i.value||Math.abs(+i.value-+v)<=0.25;const show=typed&&ok(d,r.dataset.d!)&&ok(l,r.dataset.l!);r.hidden=!show;if(show)n++;});
  if(wrap)wrap.hidden=!typed||n===0;
  if(!empty)return;
  empty.hidden=typed&&n>0;
  empty.textContent=typed?'No cartridge in this table is within 0.25 inches of that measurement. Try one number at a time, or search by part number.':'Type a diameter or a length above. Matches within 0.25 inches are listed here, each linking to its cartridge page.';
};
d.oninput=l.oninput=f;f();
</script></Base>
